# HW-021c - the CORRECT fix. 2026-07-12, COM35. PASS.
#
# Quiesce the hardware before returning the block: on the GDMA path, stop the I2S unit
# (i2s_hal_rx_stop / i2s_hal_tx_stop) before dma_stop(), and clear dma_pending. Only
# then is the in-flight block safe to hand back. Plus the TX callback must NULL
# mem_block after freeing it, or the stop-path free is a double free on tx_disable.
#
# RESULT:
#   * canary: 0 of 8 free RX blocks touched after being handed back (was 1 of 8)
#   * 100 reconfigure/START/DROP cycles, slab FLAT at 8/8 free the whole way
#   * 20 of those cycles deliberately starve TX, driving the driver down its
#     tx_disable path -- the one place the fix could double-free
#   * final census tx=8 rx=8 of 8
#
# scripts/patch_zephyr_i2s_leak.sh reproduces this driver byte for byte.
